{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will take of the spirit that is upon you and put it upon them</b> — for I will not choose them, nor will I give of My spirit upon them, for I have said that you alone shall bear them. And you said: <b>I am not able to bear all this people's burden</b> (Numbers 11:14). Choose for yourself someone who will bear with you, and you shall give of your spirit upon them. Therefore it is written: <b>And he took of the spirit that was upon him and put it upon the seventy men</b> (Numbers 11:25). But Eldad and Medad, who were not among the seventy, it is said of them: <b>and the spirit rested upon them</b> (Numbers 11:26) — meaning the spirit from HaShem, and not from Moses' own. And when Joshua said to him, <b>restrain them</b> (Numbers 11:28), he said: <b>Would that all the people of HaShem were prophets</b> (Numbers 11:29) — as though these two received when HaShem put His spirit upon them, and not like the seventy elders concerning whom it says <b>of the spirit</b> — I took of My spirit — <b>and gave it upon them.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:55.335695045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}